<Project>
  <Import Project="$([MSBuild]::GetPathOfFileAbove('Directory.Build.props', '$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)../'))" />

  <!-- #region Purpose
       Wires the repo convention analyzers (Architecture TWA*) into the runfile tools under tools/
       (dev-cli and agent-identity-cli), so those rules guard those sources directly, not only the
       files tests/tools/dev-cli-tests compile-includes. TWA0038 (500-line cap) is the
       TimeWarp.SourceGenerators rule of the same id. The root package reference applies it here too.
       #endregion

       #region Design
       Decision (Steve, task 470): the FULL convention set applies under tools/. There are exactly
       two exemptions. Do not add another here without a new decision.
       - TWA0008 is off for tools/dev-cli/services/template-smoke/ in .editorconfig, because that
         code reads and writes template tokens as strings.
       - C# content files that a NuGet package compiles into a tool are not this repo's code
         (TimeWarp.Nuru.DevCli ships its endpoints as contentFiles; two are over 500 lines).
         ExemptPackageContentFromAnalyzers below writes a global analyzer config with one section per
         Compile item under $(NuGetPackageRoot), each setting dotnet_analyzer_diagnostic.severity =
         none. That is a path exemption, with no per-file pragma, and it follows the package root
         wherever NuGet puts it. A repo .editorconfig cannot do this: its globs do not reach files
         outside the repo, and a global config section needs an absolute path, which only the build
         knows. generated_code = true was tried and rejected: it also turns off the nullable context
         for those files, so the compiler reports CS8669 on every annotation.
         Reach: the bulk key silences every rule whose severity is not set by id. It covers the TWA*
         rules and the IDE style rules. An id-level severity wins over the bulk key, so the CA rules
         that AnalysisLevel latest-all sets by id still run on those files (CA1812 does; the root
         NoWarn covers it). No config sets a TWA id severity for those paths, so TWA0038 stays off for
         package content. A config that sets one by id would bypass this exemption.
       The analyzer wiring itself is in the root Directory.Build.props, shared with source/ and
       tests/; this file opts in. tools/ is monorepo-only: the template pack project packs no tools/
       path. Under tools/ the wiring's ProjectReference form applies; its package form is reached only
       with an explicit -p:UseAnalyzerPackages=true.
       #endregion -->

  <PropertyGroup Label="Convention Analyzers">
    <EnableConventionAnalyzers>true</EnableConventionAnalyzers>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <Target Name="ExemptPackageContentFromAnalyzers"
          BeforeTargets="CoreCompile"
          Condition="'$(NuGetPackageRoot)' != ''">
    <PropertyGroup>
      <_TwPackageContentConfig>$([MSBuild]::NormalizePath('$(MSBuildProjectDirectory)', '$(IntermediateOutputPath)', 'package-content-analyzers.globalconfig'))</_TwPackageContentConfig>
      <_TwNuGetPackageRoot>$([System.String]::Copy('$(NuGetPackageRoot)').Replace('\','/'))</_TwNuGetPackageRoot>
    </PropertyGroup>
    <ItemGroup>
      <_TwPackageContentCompile Include="@(Compile->'%(FullPath)'->Replace('\','/'))" />
      <_TwPackageContentCompile Remove="@(_TwPackageContentCompile)"
                                Condition="!$([System.String]::Copy('%(Identity)').StartsWith('$(_TwNuGetPackageRoot)'))" />
      <_TwPackageContentLine Include="is_global = true" />
      <_TwPackageContentLine Include="@(_TwPackageContentCompile->'[%(Identity)]%0Adotnet_analyzer_diagnostic.severity = none')" />
    </ItemGroup>
    <WriteLinesToFile File="$(_TwPackageContentConfig)"
                      Lines="@(_TwPackageContentLine)"
                      Overwrite="true"
                      WriteOnlyWhenDifferent="true" />
    <ItemGroup>
      <EditorConfigFiles Include="$(_TwPackageContentConfig)" />
      <FileWrites Include="$(_TwPackageContentConfig)" />
    </ItemGroup>
  </Target>
</Project>
